$-------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
$ GOLAND WING MODAL ANALYSIS FOR MBDYN
$--------------------------------------------------------------------------
$
$ Updated for MSC Nastran 2024.1
$ NASTRAN model of the Goland wing. The wing is CBAR elements using
$ isotropic material properties. The mass is lumped along the span using 
$ CONM2 elements. Rigid elements (RBE2) are used to model the leading and
$ trailing edges. A clamped boundary condition is applied at the root.  
$ A SOL 103 to compute the natural frequencies and mode shapes. 
$ the end the modal mass and stiffness matrices are extracted for MBDyn 
$ using a custom ALTER. Modal shapes and static displacements are outputted 
$ in standard OP2 format for use with femgen. 
$
$ USAGE
$ Add the following lines to your BDF file:
$
$ INCLUDE 'MBDyn_NASTRAN_alter_SOL103_2024.nas' 
$ 
$ DISPLACEMENT(PLOT) = ALL $ Output displacements to .op2
$ VECTOR(PLOT) = ALL $ Output eigenvectors to .op2 
$ PARAM, OGEOM, YES $ Ensure GEOM1 in OP2 for femgen 
$ 
$ Author: Alessandro Cocco 
$          <alessandro.cocco@polimi.it>
$         Dipartimento di Ingegneria Aerospaziale - Politecnico di Milano 

INCLUDE 'MBDyn_NASTRAN_alter_SOL103_2024.nas'

CEND
  TITLE = Goland wing modal analysis for MBDyn 
  ECHO = NONE
  DISPLACEMENT(PLOT) = ALL $ Ensure displacements in OP2 for femgen
  VECTOR(PLOT) = ALL       $ Ensure eigenvectors in OP2 for femgen
  METHOD = 1
  SPC = 1
BEGIN BULK

PARAM,PRGPST,YES
PARAM,POST,-1   $ Ensure op2 output
PARAM,OGEOM,YES $ Ensure GEOM1 in OP2 for femgen
PARAM,AUTOSPC,YES
PARAM,GRDPNT,0

$.......2.......3.......4.......5.......6.......7.......8.......9.......0.......
$ Eigenanalysis data
EIGRL          1                      10       0                    MASS

$ Goland wing model 
$.......2.......3.......4.......5.......6.......7.......8.......9.......0.......
INCLUDE 'goland.blk' 

ENDDATA ed194287
